{"name":"Minions","hex":"#f3dd51","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"minions","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of minion"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/minions"}],"entries":[{"title":"Minions, Cornwall","blocks":[{"text":"Minions is a village in Cornwall, England, United Kingdom. It is situated on the eastern flank of Bodmin Moor northwest of Caradon Hill approximately four miles (6 km) north of Liskeard. Minions is first recorded in 1613 and its meaning is unknown."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Minions_-_geograph.org.uk_-_222293.jpg/330px-Minions_-_geograph.org.uk_-_222293.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minions%2C_Cornwall","wikidata":"Q11781466"},{"title":"Minions (Despicable Me)","blocks":[{"text":"Minions are a fictional all-male species of yellow capsule-shaped creatures that appear in Illumination's Despicable Me franchise, created by Eric Guillon, Pierre Coffin, and Chris Renaud. Their first appearance was in Despicable Me (2010), where they serve as the henchmen of the film's protagonist, a supervillain named Gru. The Minions are characterized by their comedic behavior and their fictional language named Minionese, which is largely unintelligible."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Minion_sculpture_in_Brisbane%2C_2024.jpg/330px-Minion_sculpture_in_Brisbane%2C_2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minions_(Despicable_Me)","wikidata":"Q15736052"},{"title":"Minions (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Minions is a 2015 American animated comedy film directed by Pierre Coffin and Kyle Balda and written by Brian Lynch. Produced by Universal Pictures and Illumination Entertainment, it is a prequel to Despicable Me (2010), the first installment in the Minions film series, and the third overall installment in the Despicable Me franchise. The film features the voices of Coffin, Sandra Bullock, Jon Hamm, Michael Keaton, Allison Janney, Steve Coogan, Jennifer Saunders, and Geoffrey Rush as the narrator. In the film, the Minions search for their replaceable evil boss after, one-by-one, accidentally killing all their past leaders throughout history."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/19/Minions_%282015_film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minions_(film)","wikidata":"Q13619743"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Minions_-_geograph.org.uk_-_222293.jpg/500px-Minions_-_geograph.org.uk_-_222293.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Minions_-_geograph.org.uk_-_222293.jpg/500px-Minions_-_geograph.org.uk_-_222293.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMinions_-_geograph.org.uk_-_222293.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Village_shop_and_post_office%2C_Minions%2C_Cornwall_-_August_2021.jpg/500px-Village_shop_and_post_office%2C_Minions%2C_Cornwall_-_August_2021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Village_shop_and_post_office%2C_Minions%2C_Cornwall_-_August_2021.jpg/1280px-Village_shop_and_post_office%2C_Minions%2C_Cornwall_-_August_2021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Village_shop_and_post_office%2C_Minions%2C_Cornwall_-_August_2021.jpg/500px-Village_shop_and_post_office%2C_Minions%2C_Cornwall_-_August_2021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","